Assist with development and oversees waste management schemes and initiatives to support re-use, recycle and disposal as necessary;
Ensure compliance with current legislation in the transportation, handling and disposal of rejects, seconds, scraps and waste;
Control costs of material disposal activities and aim to meet waste reduction and recycling targets;
Collate statistics and compile reports on rejects, seconds, scrap and waste generation and disposal;
Monitor waste & scrap levels in the entire MRM and initiate appropriate reduction action as necessary;
Ensure correct and accurate posting and transfers in ERP - SAP system;
Support Maintenance programmes to ensure machines, Cranes and other equipment are healthy;
Provide Technical support for daily facility activities. Actively participate in problem solving for safety, health and productivity improvement;
Monitor and control key consumables in Rejects handling facility;
Prepare of manpower and contractor work schedules to ensure effective and efficient processing, handling and storage of material in the facility at all times;
Ensure safe work practices and procedures at facility;
Implement training Programmes for staff;
Implement 5 K Programmes at Rejects handling facility;
Implement Continual Improvement Programmes under ISO 9001 / 14001 and Business Improvement through PIP and Health and Safety;
Implement cost reduction opportunities and Process improvements by working closely with the Operators and contractors;
Sales liaison with the sales team.
Requirements
Degree in Industrial, Mechanical or Production Engineering.
Minimum 5 years’ experience, 2 of these years must be at the Management level and 2 years’ experience at the shift engineer level.
Proficiency in ERP SAP module will be an added advantage
