Duties and responsibilities
Ensure effective and efficient running of ECDE programmes in the ward level;
Maintenance and supervision of ECDE teachers and ECDE ward staff;
Address administrative issues emanating from schools for better program management and implementation;
Monitor and evaluate the ECDE programs in the ward and mobilize local community and parents to ensure sustainability of ECDE programs;
Supervise curriculum implementation and advisory assessments in ECDE Centres in the ward;
Advocate for the needs and rights of children and ECDE programs;
Analyze and document ward ECDE data drawn from schools;
Maintain content development expertise and disseminate such knowledge to the quality assurance and standard officers and other County ECDE supervisors;
Develop and disseminate resources and best practices for the process of implementing quality improvement efforts in early childhood education;
Provide ongoing quality assurance to address children’s challenging behaviors;
Support the professional development of all staff by delivering coaching and technical assistance in the ward;
Provide guidance and support to staff with implementation of curriculum/individualization plans;
Put in place mechanisms to networking and advocacy for ECDE service providers in the ward;
Carry out other duties as shall be assigned by the sub-county ECDE program officer or any other senior county officer;
You are liable to be posted outside your ward.
Qualifications
Bachelors Degree in Early Childhood Education.
Five years relevant work experience teaching ECDE Children.
Computer literacy.
Knowledge of relevant professional standards affecting the operations especially the code of conduct for ECDE teachers.
Knowledge of the ECDE policy and legislation affecting Education in Kenya.
Terms of service is a three year (3) contract.

UNEP-GSU requests to engage a consultant who will update the ESSF and Stakeholder Response Mechanism (SRM) information on the UNEP webpages and intranet, draft communications on the ESSF and SRM and advice on a safeguards internal and external communications strategy.
Duties and Responsibilities:
Provide user-friendly navigation, layout and simple non-technical language that is relatable to the public on the UNEP safeguard pages on the Environment and Social Sustainability Framework and the Stakeholder Response Mechanism;
Develop a 2-page brochure introducing the public to the requirements of the ESSF and SRM and related tools;
Reorganize content by improving navigation, pages layouts on the Safeguards intranet pages in weCollaborate;
Qualifications/special skills
Education: Advanced (Master's degree) in international development, social science, communication or related field is required. A first-level university degree in combination with two additional years of qualifying experience may be accepted in lieu of the advanced university degree.
Experience: A minimum 5 years of work experience in report writing, training and facilitation, presentations and communication with strong research and analytical capability is required. Experience in the international organizations is desirable.
Language Requirements: English and French are the working languages of the United Nations Secretariat. For this position fluency in oral and written English is required.
Closing: 22 June 2022

